Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?comms:=20JMAP=20batch=205=20=E2=80=94=20send=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?via=20EmailSubmission=20(upload=20->=20import=20->=20submit)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires JMAP outbound send, reusing FairEmail's fully-built RFC822 MIME:
 - JmapService.sendMime: JmapClient.upload(bytes, message/rfc822) -> blobId ->
   Email/import into the Sent mailbox (seen) -> EmailSubmission/set with the
   identity whose email matches From (Identity/get). Preserves attachments +
   exact MIME (vs a structured Email/set create).
 - JmapSync.onSend: opens a JMAP connection, writes imessage to bytes, submits.
 - ServiceSend.onSend: new 'else if (protocol==TYPE_JMAP)' branch mirroring the
   MicrosoftGraph branch, so all pre/post-send bookkeeping runs unchanged.

Known-minor: Email/import also lands the message in server Sent, which the sync
pass later fetches (separate from the local sent copy) — dedup by uidl keeps
them distinct; de-dup of the local copy is a follow-up.

All rs.ltt.jmap APIs grounded from codeberg source (Uploadable, EmailImport,
ImportEmailMethodCall, SetEmailSubmissionMethodCall, GetIdentityMethodCall).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
